Changes since the July 2007 update of AmigaOS4:
- In open(), _open_r(), open64() and _open64_r() the mode is no longer
  ignored.
- utime() didn't support NULL utimebuf, fixed.
- Disabled non-working POS_ARGS in *printf().
- Now uses the file handle buffer size from DOS prefs as default buffer
  size.
- The offset in _mktm_r() with is_gmtime = 0 was wrong, fixes for
  example localtime() as well.

Changes since AmigaOS4 final:
- Added seekdir() and telldir().
- Support for shared objects added.
- Added real environment.
- Changed clock_t to 64 bit and added tm_gmtoff and tm_zone to struct
  tm.
  WARNING: Old executables will continue to work with the old types,
           but when builing new software all object files and libraries
           which use clock_t in another structure, or use struct tm or
           struct tms have to be rebuild.
- The default stdio CON: for programs started from WB now has the name
  of the program as title.
- Changed dirent functions to use IDOS->ExamineDir().
- New functions:
  llrint(), llrintf(), fdopen64(), fgetpos64(), fopen64(), fseeko64(),
  fsetpos64(), ftello64(), tmpfile64(), lseek64(), fstat64(),
  _fdopen64_r(), _fopen64_r(), _ftello64_r(), _fseeko64_r(),
  _fgetpos64_r(), _fsetpos64_r(), _tmpfile64_r(), _lseek64_r(),
  _fstat64_r(), open64(), _open64_r(), stat64(), lstat64(),
  fchmod(), fchown(), readv(), writev(), gamma(), gammaf(), lgamma()
  and lgammaf().
- No longer clears SIGBREAKF_CTRL_C if signal(SIGINT, SIG_IGN) was used.
- Several math functions have better precicion now, fixed broken
  atan2() and atan2f().
- Time functions now use timezone.library to get the UTC offset and
  dst flag.
- Updated to newlib 1.15.0.

Changes since AmigaOS pre-release Update4:
- Added error output for programs which will need newer versions of
  newlib.library.
- Added getopt_long().
- Added working getenv() and _getenv_r().
- _exit() and exit() now check if it was called by the correct process
  and use IExec->RemTask(NULL) if not.
- The memory pools used as backends for malloc(), etc. are created using
  AllocSysObjectTags() and have a name now.
- lsearch() and lfind() added.
- tmpnam(), _tmpnam_r(), tempnam(NULL,) amd _tempnam_r(,NULL,) didn't
  work for executables linked without -lunix, fixed.
- Added uname() and sys/utsname.h.
- getcwd() didn't return an unix path if linked with -lunix, fixed.
- Fixed a bug in opendir().
- Added missing INADDR_LOOPBACK define to netinet/in.h.
- Now checks if it's running in a dos process or an exec task, using
  newlib functions from exec tasks, using the global environment, is
  possible as well now. Of course using things which are not possible
  in an exec tasks wont work, for example most, if not all, file I/O.
- Added a workaround for bug #3140, there is a global fallback C library
  context now which is used if a non-newlib program is using newlib
  functions which need it, for example indirectly though a library using
  newlib.
  Since it's global it's not usable in any way, for example it's errno
  may have been changed 100 times by other code already after a function
  which sets errno is called and before it's read, it just prevents
  crashes like the one in bug #3140.
  That additionally means pr_CLibData is no longer a general C library
  data pointer but newlib-only, it either has to be set to a newlib
  context or it has to be NULL, using it for anything else will cause
  crashes now.
- Fixed a bug in fdopen().
- Replaced libc.a stubs by smaller versions.
- Added missing getlogin() to libc.a.
- Fixed an old bug in the unix->amiga path translation, for
  example "./../foobar" was translated to "foobar:" instead of
  "/foobar" (Bug #3109).
- Changed struct passwd to the one RoadShow uses.
- Replaced memory system.
- The stubs in libc.a didn't set the minmum newlib.library version to 4
  for symlink(), readlink(), basename(), dirname(), pread(), pwrite(),
  _pread_r() and _pwrite_r(), fixed.
- Added fsync().
- Added symlink(), readlink(), basename(), dirname(), pread(),
  pwrite(), _pread_r() and _pwrite_r().
- Added waitselect().
- Recreated amiga_1251.cct, cp437.cct, iso_8859_16.cct and tis_620.cct
  in the new format newlib.library 4.x uses.
- Updated to newlib 1.14.0.
- Replaced local inet_aton() by a call to ISocket->inet_aton().
- h_errno, inet_ntop(), getuid(), geteuid(), setreuid(), setuid(),
  getgid(), getegid(), setregid(), setgid(), getgroups(), setgroups(),
  initgroups(), getpwnam(), getpwuid(), setpwent(), getpwent(),
  endpwent(), getgrnam(), getgrgid(), setgrent(), getgrent(),
  endgrent(), crypt(), getpass(), setsid(), getpgrp(), getlogin()
  added.
- Changed iconv path from L:CharSets to L:CharSets/newlib.
- Added __mb_cur_max().
- It's now a kickstart module, make sure to add it to your kicklayout.
- Fixed a bug in Lib_Open().
- Removed sys/timeb.h.
- Fixed MIN() and MAX() (for GCC only).
- Added fixed netinet/in.h
- Added stdint.h.
- Reenabled sys/time.h macros.
- Added missing kill() to sys/signal.h and libc.a.
